for immediate,hexcode,value,N,Z,X in [(42,'702a4e75','0x0000002a',0,0,0),(0,'70004e75','0x00000000',0,1,1),(-1,'70ff4e75','0xffffffff',1,0,0),(-128,'70804e75','0xffffff80',1,0,1)]:
 context=f'M68000 private native fixture: bytes {hexcode}, signed immediate {immediate}, initial X={X}, D0={value}, N={N}, Z={Z}, V=0, C=0, final X={X}. RTS/private stack return checked. No game or hardware execution.'
 add('m68k-native-isa',[moveq],context,'Identify architecture and explain register/flag effects in under 65 words.',f'This is M68000 MOVEQ followed by RTS, not x86. MOVEQ sign-extends the signed 8 bit immediate {immediate} into a 32 bit D0={value}. N={N}, Z={Z}, V=0 and C=0; X stays {X}. RTS uses the supplied private return frame. This fixture establishes these CPU effects, not game or hardware correctness.')
add('m68k-native-isa',[moveq],'M68000 bytes702a4e75 decode MOVEQ #42,D0;RTS. Each instruction occupies2bytes. No complete original-source metadata exists.','Give a concise annotation; do not invent original-source provenance.','Two 2 byte M68000 instructions occupy 4 bytes. MOVEQ sets D0 to 42, clears N/Z/V/C for that nonzero positive result, and preserves X. RTS returns through the stack without changing those flags. This annotation does not recover original variable names or establish original source provenance.')
add('m68k-native-isa',[moveq],'Public verify_68000_fixture reports register values and verified private RTS return; its tool description explicitly says flags are not reported. Separate native probe reports SR for8 MOVEQ/RTS cases.','Can the public tool result alone verify X?','No. That tool reports no flag values, so its result alone cannot verify X. The instruction specification describes X preservation; the separate SR-reporting native probe checks it in the 8 declared fixtures. Keep specification, tool output and separate machine tests distinct.')
add('jaguar-tools-hooks',[proof],'Original fourthDSP checksum reads1024 bytes as16 blocks of big-endian 32 bit words. Standard MD5 compression IV/K/rounds match, but firmware adds no padding and outputs4state words in source order. Python compression/nativeDSP outputs match.','Would hashlib.md5(toc) reproduce this routine?','No. The firmware uses big-endian input words and unpadded compression across16 blocks. The standard padded MD5 byte API has different word/padding conventions. Use the source-derived compression and compare with the original DSP; do not label a standard MD5 mismatch as disproving the compression identification.')
code=(ROOT/'projects/black-ice-white-noise/restoration/biwn_firmware_TOC_checksum.c').read_text()
add('jaguar-tools-hooks',[C,proof],'Verified source contract: toc exactly1024 bytes;64 caller-supplied round_constants;4 word out. Standard MD5 IV/rounds,16big-endian blocks, no padding; unsigned modular additions and defined rotations. Return 1 on NULL input without modifying out, otherwise 0. Accepted implementation compiled C99 and matched24 native/Python cases,16 block checkpoints,3 null guards.','Return only the complete accepted portable C implementation. No fences or commentary.',code)
add('jaguar-tools-hooks',[proof],'Checksum C returns0 for nonnull pointers. Source expected header hash40ad9111f99460149c0cb36d7ef13724; actual hash1f15655720541c9daf7557e7905ad21b.','Does return0 mean disc authentication succeeded?','No. Return0 means the C calculation completed with valid pointers. Authentication requires comparing the calculated words with the expected header; the supplied values differ. Do not conflate routine status with a successful firmware authentication decision.')
add('jaguar-tools-hooks',[proof],'Accepted local-model game instruction case bodies171; a separately accepted semantic firmware checksum function1. Game components139. The semantic function is not an instruction-case body and was not integrated into the native firmware.','Report the contribution without adding unlike counts.','The local model contributed171 accepted instruction-case bodies and one separate semantic checksum function. Keep the units separate; do not report172 instruction bodies or140 game components. The checksum function has output-level comparisons, and its live firmware integration remains unverified.')
add('jaguar-tools-hooks',[proof],'C checksum matched24inputs,16baseline block checkpoints and3 null guards against originalDSP/independent compression. CPU/SSI/clocks held at captured boundaries; DSP IRQ explicitly supplied. Whole DSP state replacement was not tested.','What does this prove and what remains?','It proves the checksum output and tested null guards in those fixtures. It does not prove full DSP register/PC/IRQ state replacement, live C integration, global timing or complete firmware boot. Retain the captured-state and supplied-IRQ dependencies when reporting the result.')
add('jaguar-tools-hooks',[stage],'Source DSP loaded60000 stub bytes; originalGPU loaded1032192 stage bytes matching reference, then nativeCPU startup sampledE5E0 andDDD8. Captured resumes used. GPU bank0R31=F03FE0 supplied; its initializer unproven. BootConfig.isCDGame corrected to enable native CD frame ticks. FullC linkage/normal boot/direct4000entry trace unverified.','Summarize under 90 words and identify the next dependency.','The original processors loaded both the 60000 byte stub and the matching 1032192 byte stage, and native CPU startup was observed. This remains a diagnostic path: GPU stack input F03FE0 has no proven initializer, captured states were restored, and CD scheduling was configured explicitly. Next, resolve the stack provenance, trace the exact stage handoff and integrate the state into C startup. Full C reconstruction and normal boot remain unverified.')
add('jaguar-tools-hooks',[UI],'SDK fresh tool lookup produced a 63 word status answer in 21 seconds. Native LM Studio app selection timed out; current Chat routing refresh/test not completed. Both use the same daily model weights.','Is easy native Chat inference verified?','The SDK/tool status task worked in 21 seconds. That does not verify the native Chat window: its current routing refresh and fresh-Chat test remain pending after the UI timeout. Keep API output, saved native transcripts and current native UI verification separate.')
